          "description": "This is a Fully Remote Job\nAbout Our Client:\nThis organization operates in the AI data platform industry, addressing challenges related to sourcing and preparing proprietary, high-quality data across video, audio, text, and business workflows for AI training and evaluation. It provides a licensed platform that indexes, enriches, and packages this scarce data to support AI labs and model builders in developing next-generation AI models. The team is small but impactful, backed by top investors, and focused on solving significant bottlenecks in AI development.\nAbout the Opportunity:\nThe FRONTEND ENGINEER will build and maintain web applications used by customers and internal teams, contributing to the delivery of reliable and polished software products. The role involves working across the frontend stack, collaborating closely with design, product, and backend teams to ensure high-quality user experiences. This position is important for enabling the organization to provide effective tools and interfaces that facilitate AI data handling and modeling.\nResponsibilities:\nDevelop features for customer-facing and internal web applications in environments integrated with Rails as well as standalone frameworks\nMaintain and enhance the shared component library, including documentation and accessibility\nImplement designs with accuracy and provide constructive feedback on design specifications\nOptimize application performance focusing on rendering, bundle size, and handling large data sets\nMaintain and extend test coverage\nTroubleshoot production issues using monitoring tools\nRequirements:\nMinimum of 5 years experience building production web interfaces with React and TypeScript\nProficient in HTML, CSS, responsive layouts, and Tailwind\nSkilled at working directly from Figma files and collaborating with designers\nExperience integrating REST APIs and managing authentication and various UI states\nFamiliarity with testing frameworks such as Vitest, Jest, or Playwright\nUnderstanding of coding agents and their practical application\nClear written communication with cross-functional teams\nPay Range and Compensation Package:\nBase Salary: $130,000 to $165,000 depending on experience and location\nEquity: Competitive equity package within a well-funded AI startup\nBenefits & Perks:\nMedical, dental, and vision coverage fully paid by the employer for employees\nFlexible paid time off policy with encouragement to use it\nRemote-first work policy with occasional team offsites\nAnnual learning stipend and access to conferences\nEquity ownership with growth potential\nBudget for modern equipment and software\nEqual Opportunity Statement: Our client is an equal opportunity employer. They celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, or national origin.\nNote:\nTalentHop is a recruitment partner of this role. Please note that all employment decisions, including candidate assessment, interviews, hiring, compensation, and employment terms, are made exclusively by the hiring employer.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4486248206": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-08T22:13:46.676932+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Role Type: Full-time\nLocation: Fully Remote\nExperience: 2–3 years\nCompensation: $700 USD base salary per month, plus up to $300 USD in performance-based bonuses per month.\nAbout the Role\nSmartPropFirm is looking for a Software Development Specialist to join our Product & Engineering team.\nYou'll build, maintain, and improve software products for the prop trading industry, including trading tools, customer dashboards, rewards systems, marketplaces, and other platform features.\nWe're looking for a skilled, proactive engineer with strong technical fundamentals, practical full-stack development experience, and the ability to independently solve problems, take ownership of features, and deliver reliable solutions using modern technologies and AI-assisted development tools.\nResponsibilities\nDesign, develop, and maintain features across our web platform.\nBuild scalable, maintainable, and production-ready frontend and backend solutions.\nTake ownership of features from development through testing and deployment.\nIntegrate APIs, databases, authentication systems, and third-party services.\nIdentify and resolve bugs, performance bottlenecks, and technical issues.\nWrite clean, well-structured, reusable, and thoroughly tested code.\nConduct code reviews and contribute to improving engineering practices.\nLeverage AI development tools to accelerate development, debugging, and problem-solving.\nCollaborate with product, design, and engineering teams to deliver high-quality solutions.\nRequirements\n2–3 years of professional software development experience.\nStrong programming fundamentals and problem-solving skills.\nProficiency in JavaScript/TypeScript, React, Next.js, and Node.js.\nHands-on experience with full-stack web application development.\nSolid understanding of REST APIs, databases, authentication, and application architecture.\nExperience working with Git, code reviews, and collaborative development workflows.\nAbility to debug complex issues and optimize application performance.\nExperience using AI development tools such as ChatGPT, Cursor, Claude, or GitHub Copilot.\nStrong communication skills and the ability to work independently in a remote environment.\nAbility to take ownership of tasks and deliver high-quality work with minimal supervision.\nNice to Have\nFamiliarity with cloud services, CI/CD pipelines, and deployment workflows.\nUnderstanding of responsive UI/UX principles and frontend performance optimization.\nExperience with automated testing and production monitoring.\nExperience or interest in fintech, trading platforms, dashboards, marketplaces, or rewards systems.\nWhy Join SmartPropFirm?\nWork on real products used by traders.\nTake ownership of meaningful features and technical solutions.\nWork remotely with a collaborative, fast-moving team.\nBuild with modern technologies and AI-assisted development workflows.\nGain exposure to multiple products and complex engineering challenges.\nGrow professionally in an environment where your contributions have a direct impact.\nAdditional Requirements\n2-3+ years of hands-on experience with modern software engineering practices.\nStrong practical experience with Next.js and React.\nDemonstrated ability to independently develop, debug, and deliver production-ready features.\nComfortable working in a fully remote, collaborative development environment.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4486409930": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-08T22:13:46.676932+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Software Engineer — Pipeline Requisition\nLocation: [Remote / Hybrid / On-site]· Employment type: Full-time · Level: Engineer I through Principal\nAbout this opportunity\nSoftware Engineer - Evergreen is building a pipeline of software engineers for roles opening across our teams over the next 6–12 months. This is an evergreen posting: apply once, and our recruiters will match you to current and upcoming openings that fit your skills, level and interests.\nWe hire engineers at every stage, from early-career to principal, across product, platform, data, infrastructure, mobile, embedded and more. If you build software and want to grow with a team that values craft and curiosity, we want to hear from you, even if you don't check every box below.\nWhat you'll do\nDay-to-day work depends on the team you join, but most of our engineers:\nDesign, build, test and ship software that real people and systems depend on\nTurn ambiguous problems into clear technical plans, then deliver them in increments\nWrite maintainable code and review teammates' code with care\nCollaborate with product, design, data and operations partners\nImprove reliability, performance, security and developer experience over time\nDebug production issues and learn from them\nMentor others and share knowledge, at whatever level you're at\nTeams we hire for include web and mobile product, backend and APIs, cloud infrastructure and DevOps, data engineering and analytics, machine learning and AI, security, QA and test automation, embedded and systems, and internal tools.\nWhat we're looking for\nWe care about what you can do, not where you learned it. You'll be a strong fit if you have:\nHands-on experience writing software in at least one general-purpose language (for example Python, Java, JavaScript/TypeScript, C#, Go, C/C++, Kotlin, Swift, Ruby, Rust or PHP)\nA working grasp of programming fundamentals: data structures, algorithms, debugging and version control\nExperience building something real: a product feature, service, app, library, tool, research project or open-source contribution\nThe ability to learn new languages, frameworks and domains quickly\nClear written and spoken communication, and comfort working on a team\nExperience levels: We consider candidates with anywhere from 0 to 20+ years of experience. Your level and scope will be matched to your background during the interview process.\nEducation: A degree in computer science or a related field is welcome but not required. Equivalent experience through bootcamps, self-study, military service, apprenticeships or on-the-job learning counts just as much.\nBackgrounds we welcome\nGreat engineers come from many paths. We actively encourage applications from people who are:\nNew graduates, interns converting to full-time, and early-career engineers\nBootcamp graduates and self-taught developers\nCareer changers moving into software from science, finance, teaching, healthcare, the trades or other fields\nVeterans and transitioning service members\nReturners coming back to the workforce after a career break\nEngineers from startups, enterprises, agencies, consultancies, government, academia or open source\nSpecialists in a niche stack or domain who want to broaden, and generalists who want to go deep\nIf you meet some but not all of the qualifications, please apply anyway.\nNice to have (not required)\nNone of these are dealbreakers. They help us route you to the right team:\nCloud platforms such as AWS, Azure or Google Cloud\nFrontend frameworks (React, Angular, Vue) or mobile (iOS, Android, cross-platform)\nDatabases and data tools (SQL, NoSQL, streaming, data pipelines)\nContainers, CI/CD and infrastructure as code (Docker, Kubernetes, Terraform)\nMachine learning, LLMs or AI-assisted development workflows\nTesting, observability or security practices\nExperience in regulated or high-scale environments\nLeading projects, mentoring or managing engineers\nDisclaimer: Responsibilities may evolve as the company grows—flexibility is key. This position is part of LinkedIn’s Full-Service Hiring beta program and is open to candidates performing services in the U.S. (excluding AK, HI, NV, SC, and WV). We’re committed to making our hiring process as smooth and timely as possible, and we understand that waiting to hear back can add to the anticipation. If you’re a potential fit, our team will reach out within two weeks to progress you to the next stage. If you don’t hear from us in that time, we encourage you to explore other opportunities with our team in the future, and we wish you the very best in your job search.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4486639685": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-08T22:13:46.676932+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "The Role:\nBuild features end-to-end on the deals module. You'll own everything from backend APIs to polished frontend experiences.\nWhat You'll Do:\n- Build REST APIs in Laravel 12: controllers, Form Request validation, Eloquent models, migrations, queues\n- Implement access control: roles and permissions (Spatie), JWT verification of tokens issued by central identity service (RS256, JWKS)\n- Build React 18 / TypeScript screens with Vite, React Query, React Router and Tailwind; integrate Microsoft sign-in (MSAL)\n- Integrate with other services over REST: user and role sync, signed service tokens, AI services\n- Write tests (PHPUnit / Pest, Vitest, Cypress) and review pull requests\nMust Have:\n- 4+ years full-stack (Laravel and React)\n- PHP 8.2+, Laravel 10-12: Eloquent, migrations, queues, Sanctum or JWT auth\n- MySQL 8: schema design, indexes, query tuning\n- React 18, TypeScript 5, hooks, React Query (TanStack), React Router\n- REST API design, OpenAPI / Swagger; Git and pull-request workflow\n- Testing on both sides: PHPUnit or Pest; Vitest or Jest\nNice to Have:\n- OAuth2 / OpenID Connect, Microsoft Entra ID, MSAL\n- Docker, Redis; Azure (App Service, Key Vault, Front Door); GitHub Actions\n- Tailwind CSS, Radix / shadcn UI, Tiptap; Java / Spring Boot exposure\nStack: PHP 8.2+ • Laravel 12 • MySQL 8 • React 18 • TypeScript 5 • Vite • Azure",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4486798301": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-08T22:13:46.676932+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About The Role\nThe Frontend Engineer role owns the client-facing surface of the product — building fast, accessible interfaces that thousands of users interact with daily. The team ships production React and TypeScript code across a modern SPA architecture, with real ownership over component libraries, state management patterns, and rendering performance.\nThe role sits at the intersection of design and infrastructure: translating Figma specs into pixel-accurate, tested UI while collaborating with backend engineers on API contracts and GraphQL/REST integration. Every feature shipped by this team is visible to users within a sprint.\nKey Responsibilities\nBuild and maintain user-facing features in React and TypeScript, delivering production-ready components on a two-week release cycle\nDesign and evolve a shared component library with Storybook, enforcing accessibility standards (WCAG 2.1 AA) across the product surface\nOptimize frontend performance: bundle analysis, code splitting, lazy loading, and Core Web Vitals tuning for applications serving high daily traffic\nIntegrate REST and GraphQL APIs, owning data-fetching layers and client-side caching strategy (React Query, Apollo, or similar)\nWrite comprehensive unit and integration tests with Jest, React Testing Library, and Playwright; maintain CI pipelines that gate merges on coverage\nCollaborate directly with product designers to review specs, flag technical constraints early, and prototype interaction details\nParticipate in code reviews, architecture discussions, and incident triage when frontend issues reach production\nWhat We Are Looking For\n3–6 years of professional frontend engineering experience building and maintaining production web applications\nDeep expertise in React, TypeScript, and modern JavaScript (ES6+), with strong opinions on component architecture and state management (Redux, Zustand, or equivalent)\nHands-on experience with CSS-in-JS or utility frameworks (Tailwind, styled-components) and building responsive, accessible layouts\nProven track record diagnosing and fixing performance bottlenecks — rendering, bundling, network — using DevTools and profiling tools\nExperience with automated testing at multiple levels and integrating frontend builds into CI/CD pipelines\nBachelor's degree in Computer Science or equivalent practical experience\nBonus: experience with Next.js or server-side rendering, design system ownership, WebGL/data visualization, or contributing to open-source frontend tooling",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4486920084": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-08T22:13:46.676932+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Job Title: Python Developer\nLocation: (Remote)\nJob Type: Full-Time\nExperience Level: Entry to Junior (1–3 Years)\nAbout the Role\nWe are looking for a motivated and technically skilled Python Developer with 1–3 years of experience to join our growing development team. This role is ideal for early-career professionals interested in building scalable applications, developing backend services, and working with modern Python frameworks.\nThe Python Developer will work closely with software engineers, technical leads, QA teams, and business stakeholders to develop, test, maintain, and enhance software applications and backend solutions.\nKey Responsibilities\nDesign, develop, test, and maintain applications using Python .\nWrite clean, reusable, efficient, and maintainable code following development best practices.\nDevelop backend services, APIs, and application components using frameworks such as Django, Flask, or FastAPI .\nBuild and integrate RESTful APIs and web services.\nWork with relational and NoSQL databases to manage and retrieve application data.\nWrite and optimize SQL queries and support database integration.\nIdentify, troubleshoot, and resolve application bugs and performance issues.\nDevelop unit tests and support integration testing to ensure software quality.\nCollaborate with frontend developers, QA engineers, and technical teams to deliver application features.\nParticipate in code reviews and follow coding standards and version control practices.\nSupport application deployment, maintenance, and debugging activities.\nParticipate in Agile/Scrum meetings, sprint planning, and technical discussions.\nMaintain technical documentation and stay updated with emerging Python technologies and development practices.\nBasic Qualifications\nBachelor's degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Software Engineering, or a related field .\n1–3 years of experience in Python development or software engineering.\nStrong knowledge of Python programming, object-oriented programming, and data structures .\nFamiliarity with Python frameworks such as Django, Flask, or FastAPI .\nUnderstanding of REST APIs, web services, and backend development concepts.\nBasic knowledge of SQL and relational databases such as MySQL or PostgreSQL.\nFamiliarity with Git, GitHub, or GitLab.\nUnderstanding of software development lifecycle (SDLC), debugging, and testing.\nStrong analytical, problem-solving, and communication skills.\nAbility to work independently and collaborate with cross-functional teams.\nPreferred Skills\nExperience developing and integrating RESTful APIs.\nFamiliarity with frontend technologies such as HTML, CSS, JavaScript, or React.\nKnowledge of databases such as PostgreSQL, MySQL, MongoDB, or SQL Server .\nBasic understanding of cloud platforms such as AWS, Microsoft Azure, or GCP .\nExposure to Docker, Kubernetes, and CI/CD pipelines.\nFamiliarity with Python libraries such as Pandas, NumPy, Requests, or Pytest .\nUnderstanding of microservices architecture and application integration.\nExperience with automated testing and application performance optimization.\nFamiliarity with Agile/Scrum methodologies and tools such as Jira and Confluence.\nBasic knowledge of Linux/Unix environments.\nAcademic, personal, or professional projects demonstrating practical Python development skills.\nWhat You'll Gain\nOpportunity to work on real-world Python development and software engineering projects .\nHands-on experience with Python frameworks, backend development, APIs, and databases.\nExposure to cloud technologies, application deployment, and modern development tools.\nPractical experience with software testing, debugging, and collaborative development.\nMentorship from experienced Python Developers and technical professionals.\nOpportunities to strengthen skills in backend development, automation, and application engineering.\nCareer growth opportunities toward Python Developer, Backend Developer, Full-Stack Developer, Software Engineer, and Senior Python Developer roles.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4485584642": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-08T18:00:13.664744+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Position: Freelance Computer Programmer – Code Review & System Optimization\nDepartment: Information Technology\nProject: DT Brain\nEmployment Type: Freelance / Project-Based\nReporting To: Chief Technology Officer (CTO)\nCompany: Dany Tameerat\nJob Overview\nDany Tameerat is seeking a skilled and experienced Freelance Computer Programmer to conduct a comprehensive technical review, optimization, and enhancement of DT Brain, the company's integrated business management system.\nDT Brain supports multiple business functions, including Sales CRM, Finance, Human Resources, Payroll, Project Management, Recruitment, and Executive Reporting.\nThe ideal candidate will possess strong programming expertise, with proven experience in reviewing existing codebases, identifying technical gaps, resolving performance and security issues, and implementing sustainable improvements to enhance overall system efficiency, reliability, and maintainability.\nKey Responsibilities\n1. Code Review & Technical Assessment\nConduct a comprehensive review of the existing application codebase.\nIdentify technical deficiencies, vulnerabilities, inefficiencies, and areas requiring improvement.\nProvide a prioritized assessment of recommended fixes and upgrades.\n2. System Performance & Optimization\nIdentify and resolve performance bottlenecks across application pages, database queries, and background processes.\nOptimize database queries, indexing, and overall application responsiveness.\nImprove system efficiency without disrupting existing business operations.\n3. Application Security & Reliability\nAssess authentication mechanisms, role-based access controls, data handling, and software dependencies.\nIdentify and address potential security vulnerabilities in accordance with established web application security practices.\nStrengthen system stability, reliability, and data protection.\n4. Code Quality & System Enhancement\nRefactor and restructure existing code to improve readability, scalability, and maintainability.\nImplement necessary technical upgrades while preserving existing system functionality.\nRecommend improvements aligned with long-term system requirements.\n5. Testing & Quality Assurance\nReview existing automated test coverage and ensure current test suites remain functional.\nDevelop additional tests where necessary to validate system improvements.\nIdentify and resolve defects introduced or discovered during the optimization process.\n6. Technical Documentation & Handover\nMaintain clear documentation of technical findings, modifications, and implemented improvements.\nSubmit a concise technical assessment and completion report.\nProvide recommendations for future system enhancements and maintenance.\nRequired Qualifications & Skills\nDemonstrated professional experience in software development, programming, and maintaining web-based applications.\nStrong proficiency in one or more programming languages, with the ability to understand and work with existing application architectures.\nPractical experience with Python, Flask, and Jinja-based applications , or demonstrable ability to work effectively with this technology stack.\nStrong understanding of relational databases, including SQLite or SQL-based systems, query optimization, and indexing.\nWorking knowledge of JavaScript, HTML, and CSS.\nProven expertise in code auditing, debugging, refactoring, performance optimization, and technical troubleshooting.\nFamiliarity with automated testing frameworks, including pytest or equivalent tools.\nUnderstanding of web application security principles, authentication, authorization, and OWASP Top 10.\nStrong analytical, problem-solving, documentation, and communication skills.\nPreferred Qualifications\nPrevious experience working with ERP, CRM, finance, or enterprise business management applications.\nFamiliarity with Windows-based server environments and scheduled background processes.\nKnowledge of Node.js or additional web development technologies.\nExperience independently reviewing and upgrading existing business-critical applications.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4485704382": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-08T18:00:13.664744+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Dengage is a multinational SaaS company dedicated to delivering innovative solutions that drive digital engagement and enhance customer experiences. Our team is passionate about technology and committed to fostering an environment where talent can thrive and grow.\nWe are looking for a talented and motivated Full Stack Developer to join our engineering team and contribute to the development, enhancement, and maintenance of our SaaS platform.\nKey Responsibilities\nDesign, develop, and maintain scalable web applications using modern frontend and backend technologies.\nDevelop responsive, user-friendly interfaces using JavaScript, TypeScript, Vue.js, React, or similar frameworks.\nBuild and maintain backend applications, services, and RESTful APIs using C#, .NET Core, or similar technologies.\nDesign, develop, and optimize relational databases, including SQL Server or PostgreSQL.\nIntegrate frontend applications with backend services and third-party APIs.\nWrite clean, efficient, reusable, and maintainable code following software development best practices.\nTroubleshoot, debug, and resolve application performance and functionality issues.\nParticipate in code reviews, technical discussions, and system design activities.\nCollaborate with product managers, QA engineers, and other developers to deliver high-quality features.\nImplement appropriate security, authentication, and authorization mechanisms.\nWrite and maintain unit tests and integration tests.\nParticipate in Agile/Scrum development processes and contribute to continuous improvement.\nSupport application deployment, monitoring, and ongoing optimization.\nRequirements\nTechnical Skills\nBachelor's degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Information Technology, or a related field.\n3–5 years of professional experience in full stack software development.\nStrong understanding of object-oriented programming (OOP), data structures, and software development principles.\nHands-on experience with C#, ASP.NET Core, .NET Core, or similar backend frameworks.\nStrong proficiency in JavaScript, TypeScript, HTML5, and CSS3.\nPractical experience with Vue.js, React.js, or similar frontend frameworks.\nExperience developing and integrating RESTful APIs.\nGood understanding of relational databases, SQL queries, and database optimization.\nFamiliarity with Entity Framework Core or other ORM frameworks.\nExperience with Git and collaborative development workflows.\nUnderstanding of authentication, authorization, and web application security.\nFamiliarity with Agile software development methodologies.\nStrong debugging, analytical, and problem-solving skills.\nGood communication skills and ability to work effectively within a team.\nPreferred / Nice-to-Have Skills\nPrevious experience developing SaaS products or cloud-based applications.\nExperience with Microsoft Azure, AWS, or other cloud platforms.\nFamiliarity with Docker, containerization, and CI/CD pipelines.\nUnderstanding of microservices architecture and distributed systems.\nExperience with Redis, MongoDB, or other NoSQL databases.\nKnowledge of message queues such as RabbitMQ or Kafka.\nFamiliarity with automated testing frameworks.\nExperience working with high-volume data processing applications.\nExposure to marketing technology (MarTech), customer engagement platforms, or customer data platforms (CDP).\nBasic understanding of application performance monitoring and optimization.\nBenefits\nBenefits\nGrowth Opportunities: Access to professional development and career growth within a rapidly expanding SaaS company.\nCollaborative Culture: Work in a supportive and innovative environment where your contributions are valued.\nCompetitive Benefits: Enjoy a comprehensive benefits package.\nD.engage is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all Team Members.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4485876213": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-08T18:00:13.664744+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Want to learn more about this role and Jobot? Click our Jobot logo and follow\nour LinkedIn page!\nJob details:\nAI Software Engineer, $100,000 to $130,000 base; potential 10% annual bonus, AI-Assisted and Agentic Coding, Support from Senior Engineers\nThis Jobot Job is hosted by: Alex Dickinson\nAre you a fit? Easy Apply now by clicking the \"Easy Apply\" button\nand sending us your resume.\nSalary: $100,000 - $130,000 per year\nA bit about us:\nWe are a digital media business focused on physicians, working at the point where pharmaceutical brands and healthcare professionals meet. Our work centers on building personalized engagement programs that help pharmaceutical brands connect with doctors and other healthcare professionals. Those programs run across multiple channels, so brands can reach clinicians in the places they already spend their time.\nWhy join us?\nCompetitive compensation: $100,000 to $130,000 base; potential 10% annual bonus\n401(k) plan with company match\nComprehensive benefits, including health, dental, life, accident and disability insurance, plus a prescription plan and flexible spending account\nPaid holidays and vacation, along with sick days and a personal day\nHands-on AI-assisted and agentic coding work, backed by senior engineers\nOwnership scope that grows over time\nInternships and personal projects count toward your experience\nJob Details\nYou'll build product features for a digital platform used by physicians, taking on more independent ownership over time, while also helping shape the repository setup and review practices that make AI-assisted and agentic coding dependable.\nKey Responsibilities:\nDeliver product features for the physician-facing platform, growing into more independent ownership as you go\nHelp design software systems and review code written by other engineers\nWrite maintainable applications backed by automated tests, clean code, peer review and clear documentation\nSupport the platform's performance, security and compliance\nSet up the repository context, conventions, automated tests, quality gates and executable plans that keep agentic coding reliable\nExamine AI-generated plans and code with a critical eye and raise any issues you find\nSpot repetitive or time-consuming engineering tasks that can shift to AI-assisted or automated workflows, keeping human review in place where it safeguards quality and compliance\nTrack down and fix bugs in pre-production and production environments, with help from senior engineers\nPartner with engineering and non-engineering colleagues on team and company goals\nTake part in company-wide projects alongside other business units\nNeeded:\nAssociate or bachelor's degree in computer science or a related field, or equivalent software engineering experience\nMinimum 1 year of software development experience (internships, co-ops, academic, open-source or substantial personal projects all count)\nHands-on experience with AI coding assistants, including reviewing and correcting what they produce\nTypeScript\nReact\nPython\nSQL and relational databases\nGit version control\nExperience with at least one major cloud platform (AWS, GCP or Vercel)\nA GitHub profile or portfolio that shows hands-on development work\nAuthorization to work in the US without visa sponsorship\nInterested in hearing more? Easy Apply now by clicking the \"Easy Apply\" button.\nJobot is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We provide an inclusive work environment that celebrates diversity and all qualified candidates receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, national origin, age (40 and over), disability, military status, genetic information or any other basis protected by applicable federal, state, or local laws. Jobot also prohibits harassment of applicants or employees based on any of these protected categories. It is Jobot’s policy to comply with all applicable federal, state and local laws respecting consideration of unemployment status in making hiring decisions.\nSometimes Jobot is required to perform background checks with your authorization. Jobot will consider qualified candidates with criminal histories in a manner consistent with any applicable federal, state, or local law regarding criminal backgrounds, including but not limited to the Los Angeles Fair Chance Initiative for Hiring and the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance.\nInformation collected and processed as part of your Jobot candidate profile, and any job applications, resumes, or other information you choose to submit is subject to Jobot's Privacy Policy, as well as the Jobot California Worker Privacy Notice and Jobot Notice Regarding Automated Employment Decision Tools which are available at jobot.com/legal.\nBy applying for this job, you agree to receive calls, AI-generated calls, text messages, or emails from Jobot, and/or its agents and contracted partners. Frequency varies for text messages. Message and data rates may apply. Carriers are not liable for delayed or undelivered messages. You can reply STOP to cancel and HELP for help. You can access our privacy policy here: jobot.com/privacy-policy\nWant to learn more about this role\nand Jobot?\nClick our Jobot logo and follow our LinkedIn page!",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4487759912": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-08T18:00:13.664744+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About the Role\nStartupSphere is seeking a Node.js Developer to design, build, and deliver software serving millions of users every day. Based in Anchorage, Alaska, the company is moving toward a remote-native working environment focused on ownership, collaboration, and professional growth.\nThis role offers the opportunity to take ownership of projects, contribute to technology initiatives, and work with a supportive team. The ideal candidate has at least one year of relevant experience, understands technology best practices, and is comfortable taking initiative to identify problems and develop effective solutions.\nKey Responsibilities\nCollaborate with QA teams to define test coverage and identify regressions early.\nMaintain code quality through automated linting, testing, and static analysis.\nIdentify data-driven Interpersonal Skills regressions in staging before they affect Anchorage customers.\nEvaluate existing values-led Interpersonal Skills patterns and recommend cleaner alternatives.\nCoordinate releases with stakeholders across Anchorage, Alaska, and remote teams.\nDevelop Terraform integration tests to identify regressions before releases in Anchorage, Alaska.\nSupport the migration of StartupSphere's Laravel stack out of the Alaska region before the migration deadline.\nRequired Qualifications\n1+ years of relevant experience in technology-related roles.\nStrong attention to detail and the ability to distinguish completed work from work that still needs improvement.\nPattern recognition skills developed through multiple technology engagements.\nAbility to communicate data-driven insights and translate them into actionable decisions.\nAt least one year of experience navigating the challenges and stakeholder dynamics associated with technology projects.\nStrong sense of ownership and accountability for project outcomes.\nSolid understanding of technology best practices and industry standards.\nAbility to take initiative and resolve problems independently.\nCompensation & Benefits\nSalary: $76,000–$109,000.\nGenerous benefits package.\nOpportunities to lead projects and develop professional skills.\nWork Arrangement & Location\nCompany Location: Anchorage, Alaska.\nWork Arrangement: Remote-native working environment.\nLocation Coordination: Collaboration with stakeholders across Anchorage, Alaska, and remote teams.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      }
    },
